<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>World news and headlines - RFI</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events in France, Europe and around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/</link><lastBuildDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 15:55:44 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>International</category><title>UAE building ‘relationships of dependence’ through investment across Africa</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260829-uae-building-relationships-of-dependence-through-investment-across-africa</link><description>
The United Arab Emirates has become a major economic and strategic force in Africa, through investments in key sectors and a growing involvement in conflicts on the continent – prompting some to describe its approach as imperialist.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/afe57ed2-fc89-11f0-aa8b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-9WF3QY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/afe57ed2-fc89-11f0-aa8b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-9WF3QY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aa6fdd7e-a087-11f1-85a0-bfda8eb3ae4b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 15:54:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/afe57ed2-fc89-11f0-aa8b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-9WF3QY.jpg">© Ed Ram/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Trapped for 115 days, cargo ship captain recounts ordeal in Strait of Hormuz</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260829-trapped-for-115-days-cargo-ship-captain-recounts-ordeal-in-strait-of-hormuz</link><description>
In late January 2026, the Banglar Joyjatra, a Bangladeshi bulk carrier, entered the Persian Gulf on what should have been a routine commercial voyage before continuing to South Africa. Instead, Captain Mohammad Shafiqul Islam and his crew became trapped for 115 days as conflict engulfed the Strait of Hormuz. He told RFI how the voyage turned into a fight to get his ship and crew safely out.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/db1308ce-a2e5-11f1-8aa6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Banglar-Joyjatra-reformatted.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/db1308ce-a2e5-11f1-8aa6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Banglar-Joyjatra-reformatted.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6591e54-a2cc-11f1-a569-398d216dac62</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 09:16:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/db1308ce-a2e5-11f1-8aa6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Banglar-Joyjatra-reformatted.jpg">© Bangladesh Shipping Corporation</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Iceland referendum could put EU membership talks back on the table</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260829-iceland-referendum-could-put-eu-membership-talks-back-on-the-table</link><description>
Icelanders will vote on Saturday on whether to resume negotiations to join the European Union, with the result expected to be finely balanced after a campaign dominated by questions of sovereignty, fishing and the country’s place in an increasingly uncertain geopolitical landscape.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/191829e8-a29a-11f1-bd56-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239717725586.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/191829e8-a29a-11f1-bd56-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239717725586.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">32d2da14-a2b7-11f1-8c72-7d8b04e91d75</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 06:50:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/191829e8-a29a-11f1-bd56-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239717725586.jpg">© AP Photo/Marco Di Marco</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Rescuers claw through mud as missing toll from Nepal, China flood nears 3,000</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260829-rescuers-claw-through-mud-as-missing-toll-from-nepal-china-flood-nears-3-000</link><description>
Rescuers in Nepal and China were battling on Saturday to locate thousands of people missing days after a deadly, tsunami-like wall of water and debris swept through the Himalayan region, engulfing entire villages.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5208577c-a34a-11f1-83de-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/a829ecd6ae49241a9bcfea704553a75d5f0763c6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5208577c-a34a-11f1-83de-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/a829ecd6ae49241a9bcfea704553a75d5f0763c6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5305fc56-a34a-11f1-8692-77fc6b06ebe5</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 01:38:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5208577c-a34a-11f1-83de-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/a829ecd6ae49241a9bcfea704553a75d5f0763c6.jpg">© MANAN VATSYAYANA / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>‘Words and promises not enough’ as Syria’s Kurds face uncertain future</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260828-words-and-promises-are-not-enough-as-syria-s-kurds-face-uncertain-future</link><description>
Syria’s Kurds are facing an uncertain future after this week’s dissolution of the Kurdish-led Syrian Democratic Forces and the integration of military and civilian institutions in northeastern Syria into the Syrian state, raising questions over what the changes will mean for their rights, safety and daily lives. RFI spoke to a Kurdish civil society activist in the region.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8842c9ae-a222-11f1-a5b3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4B68KG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8842c9ae-a222-11f1-a5b3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4B68KG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7b92699e-a218-11f1-8110-418826f8ad24</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 16:05:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8842c9ae-a222-11f1-a5b3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4B68KG.jpg">AFP - DELIL SOULEIMAN</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Serb war criminal Mladic, dubbed the ‘Butcher of Bosnia,’ dies aged 84</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260827-bosnian-serb-war-criminal-dubbed-the-butcher-of-bosnia-dies-aged-84</link><description>
Ratko Mladic, the former Bosnian Serb military chief convicted of war crimes for his role in the 1995 Srebrenica massacre, died in hospital on Thursday, according to a United Nations international tribunal.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d2d1841a-a22c-11f1-96f9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T142848Z-1358587860-RC227NA3MIE4-RTRMADP-3-PEOPLE-RATKO-MLADIC-REACTIONS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d2d1841a-a22c-11f1-96f9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T142848Z-1358587860-RC227NA3MIE4-RTRMADP-3-PEOPLE-RATKO-MLADIC-REACTIONS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ac9259c4-a230-11f1-8f4a-8f6ffdc70ead</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 16:02:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d2d1841a-a22c-11f1-96f9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T142848Z-1358587860-RC227NA3MIE4-RTRMADP-3-PEOPLE-RATKO-MLADIC-REACTIONS.jpg">©  Chris Helgren / Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Nepal’s deadly glacier collapse exposes climate risks across the Himalayas</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260827-nepal-s-deadly-glacier-collapse-exposes-climate-risks-across-the-himalayas</link><description>
A massive glacier collapse that triggered deadly flooding on the Nepal-Tibet border has exposed the growing dangers facing the rapidly warming Himalayas, where scientists say retreating ice and thawing ground are making mountain landscapes increasingly unstable.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4310f710-a20a-11f1-bc15-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T020731Z-574437780-RC2P6NAPHNWT-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4310f710-a20a-11f1-bc15-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T020731Z-574437780-RC2P6NAPHNWT-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e5c1da20-a222-11f1-af26-f7f1b19f1d48</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 16:01:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4310f710-a20a-11f1-bc15-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T020731Z-574437780-RC2P6NAPHNWT-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg">© REUTERS - Navesh Chitrakar </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Haiti families plead for release of hostages after deadly gang attack</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260827-haiti-families-plead-for-release-of-hostages-after-deadly-gang-attack</link><description>
Families in Kenscoff near the Haitian capital Port-au-Prince are demanding the release of relatives taken hostage by armed gangs during last weekend's deadly attack on the town. At least 47 people were killed and more than 20 abducted, with thousands having fled their homes to avoid further attacks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/60da7c5c-a1cf-11f1-94b7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-24T205531Z-633498750-RC225NAK43KW-RTRMADP-3-HAITI-VIOLENCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/60da7c5c-a1cf-11f1-94b7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-24T205531Z-633498750-RC225NAK43KW-RTRMADP-3-HAITI-VIOLENCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e25ceed8-a204-11f1-937e-4918512faead</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 14:02:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/60da7c5c-a1cf-11f1-94b7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-24T205531Z-633498750-RC225NAK43KW-RTRMADP-3-HAITI-VIOLENCE.jpg">REUTERS - Patrice Noel</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>EU joins aid effort as more than 1,300 remain missing after Nepal floods</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260827-eu-sends-help-as-nepal-flood-kills-165-hundreds-of-tourists-remain-missing</link><description>
The EU has joined international efforts to send aid after catastrophic floods on the Nepal-Tibet border left at least 360 people dead and more than 1,300 missing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7470e99e-a194-11f1-93c6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-26T134117Z-100630411-RC2D6NA8CH3P-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7470e99e-a194-11f1-93c6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-26T134117Z-100630411-RC2D6NA8CH3P-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">955bd734-a1e1-11f1-98ba-5b8c9d49903f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 06:36:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7470e99e-a194-11f1-93c6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-26T134117Z-100630411-RC2D6NA8CH3P-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg">© Navesh Chitraka/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>How Dolly Parton became much more than country music’s 'backwoods Barbie'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260825-how-dolly-parton-became-much-more-than-country-music-s-backwoods-barbie</link><description>
Back in 2008 at age 62, Dolly Parton released a single proclaiming she was "just a backwoods Barbie, too much makeup, too much hair."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/57f47062-a0b1-11f1-bfdf-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/b1eafd7dce9336939880e6ee32dd960e7e66b898.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/57f47062-a0b1-11f1-bfdf-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/b1eafd7dce9336939880e6ee32dd960e7e66b898.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">58e35876-a0b1-11f1-9051-87f52546a6be</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 18:18:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/57f47062-a0b1-11f1-bfdf-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/b1eafd7dce9336939880e6ee32dd960e7e66b898.jpg">© Robyn Beck / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>'Shocking' book about Putin's private life wins French literary prize</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260825-shocking-book-about-putin-s-private-life-wins-french-literary-prize</link><description>
A taboo-breaking book about Vladimir Putin's rise to power and private life, written by two exiled Russian journalists, won a newly established French literary prize on Tuesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1da653fe-8530-11f1-b1cb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T164544Z-2032476191-RC2LHMAO5MSC-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-PUTIN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1da653fe-8530-11f1-b1cb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T164544Z-2032476191-RC2LHMAO5MSC-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-PUTIN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">56adb7b2-a09e-11f1-8d4d-b97a63a72a51</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 16:02:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1da653fe-8530-11f1-b1cb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T164544Z-2032476191-RC2LHMAO5MSC-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-PUTIN.jpg">via REUTERS - Alexander Kazakov</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>US and Denmark push for nationwide expansion of UN arms embargo in Sudan</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260825-us-and-denmark-push-for-nationwide-expansion-of-un-arms-embargo-in-sudan</link><description>
The United States on Monday urged the United Nations Security Council to expand an arms embargo on the Sudanese region of Darfur to cover all of Sudan, saying the nation's brutal conflict risks regional expansion. The suggestion was supported by Denmark, which holds the Council's rotating presidency. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/09831f54-2d95-11f0-9636-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25123519167407.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/09831f54-2d95-11f0-9636-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25123519167407.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d45c51f4-a081-11f1-a5dd-bfda8eb3ae4b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 15:00:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/09831f54-2d95-11f0-9636-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25123519167407.jpg">© AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>At least 40 killed as gangs attack displaced people near Haiti capital</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260825-at-least-40-killed-as-gangs-attack-displaced-people-near-haiti-capital</link><description>
At least 40 people have been killed, some execution-style, after gangs attacked displaced people sheltering in a church near Haiti's capital Port-au-Prince at the weekend, local authorities said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dd5c43a8-a019-11f1-aa1f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236704099772.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dd5c43a8-a019-11f1-aa1f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236704099772.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8485013a-a059-11f1-9823-679e8866c115</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 08:53:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dd5c43a8-a019-11f1-aa1f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236704099772.jpg">© AP Photo/Odelyn Joseph</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Namibia paves way for phosphate mining in the Atlantic Ocean</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260825-namibia-paves-way-for-phosphate-mining-in-the-atlantic-ocean</link><description>
Namibia has granted environmental clearance for an offshore phosphate mining project that paves the way for the world's first commercial seabed-dredging operation for the mineral, despite opposition from green groups and the fishing industry.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/51fdb99a-a046-11f1-bb8a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ed9e94009377e5e8e0ade5ed52204e6e27aa4874.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/51fdb99a-a046-11f1-bb8a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ed9e94009377e5e8e0ade5ed52204e6e27aa4874.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">52cbf148-a046-11f1-bc5f-2b4787bb34a0</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 05:32:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/51fdb99a-a046-11f1-bb8a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ed9e94009377e5e8e0ade5ed52204e6e27aa4874.jpg">© MARCO LONGARI / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Ukraine's allies pledge to continue support with focus on air defence</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260824-ukraine-s-allies-pledge-to-continue-support-with-focus-on-air-defence</link><description>
Ukraine's allies on Monday pledged to keep up their support in the war against Russia, with a renewed focus on air defence investment to counter a shortage of US Patriot interceptors. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/71afd38c-9fa5-11f1-af79-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236363361580.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/71afd38c-9fa5-11f1-af79-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236363361580.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f9103d0e-9fe5-11f1-8ca1-af870d26e276</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 19:17:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/71afd38c-9fa5-11f1-af79-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236363361580.jpg">© Henry Nicholls / Pool AFP via AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Saudi Arabia to invest €6bn in building theme parks near Paris</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260824-saudi-arabia-to-invest-7-bn-in-theme-parks-near-paris-french-presidency</link><description>
France and Saudi Arabia on Monday signed a memo of understanding for a €6 billion Saudi investment to create three theme parks near Paris, the office of the French president said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c4cc18b4-9fe6-11f1-bfdc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/e5bef9e73595ec0265cbf9aa320acbe08d2c098a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c4cc18b4-9fe6-11f1-bfdc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/e5bef9e73595ec0265cbf9aa320acbe08d2c098a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c5e83b10-9fe6-11f1-a438-af870d26e276</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 18:08:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c4cc18b4-9fe6-11f1-bfdc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/e5bef9e73595ec0265cbf9aa320acbe08d2c098a.jpg">© LOU BENOIST / POOL/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Looking up: Hunting stars and nebulae from the peaks of the French Alps</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260824-looking-up-hunting-stars-and-nebulae-from-the-peaks-of-the-french-alps</link><description>
French astronaut Sophie Adenot made history this month as the first French woman to perform a spacewalk. Back on Earth, space enthusiasts across France are finding their own ways to reach for the stars. In a five-part series this week, RFI meets some of them. First up is astrophotographer Aude Nowak, who climbs high into the French Alps to capture stars, nebulae and the Milky Way.
